## What

Implement the **Individual-validated** S/MIME tier as a Profile type in `pkix-profiles-cabf`. Per CA/B Forum S/MIME BR §7.6.x: strictest non-organization tier; requires real-world identity proofing (passport / national ID / driver's license per BR §6.x evidence requirements).

## API shape

```rust
/// Individual-validated S/MIME BR subscriber-certificate profile.
///
/// Reference, not authoritative. CA/B Forum S/MIME Baseline Requirements
/// v1.0.14 (or whichever revision the cabf workspace has refreshed to).
///
/// Asserts policy OID `2.23.140.1.5.4.1` (Individual-validated).
///
/// Required Subject DN fields per BR: givenName + surname (or pseudonym),
/// serialNumber (subject-unique identifier). No organizationName required.
/// Subject SAN: rfc822Name (one or more).
pub struct SmimeIndividualValidated;

impl Profile for SmimeIndividualValidated {
    fn policy(&self, now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
        // - required_leaf_eku: id-kp-emailProtection
        // - require_rfc822_san: true
        // - max_validity: per BR §6.3.2
        // - required_policy_oids: [2.23.140.1.5.4.1]
        // - required_subject_dn_attributes: [givenName + surname]
    }
    fn version(&self) -> &'static str { "1.0.14" }
}

pub const fn smime_individual_policy(now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
    SmimeIndividualValidated.policy(now_unix)
}
```

## Test fixtures

Same dual-oracle convention. Note: Individual-validated is the rarest tier in practice, so fixture availability from zlint testdata / pkilint fixtures may be thinner. If both upstreams lack fixtures, fall back to hand-generating certs cross-verified against both linters in subprocess (composed-oracle pattern per memory `pkix-composed-oracle-pattern-2026-05-13`).

## Acceptance

- [ ] `pkix_profiles_cabf::SmimeIndividualValidated` ships and impls `Profile`
- [ ] `smime_individual_policy(now_unix)` free function alias exists
- [ ] Reference-not-authoritative rustdoc disclaimer
- [ ] Rustdoc cites CA/B Forum S/MIME BR v1.0.14 with correct section numbers (post-PKIX-d5rh refresh)
- [ ] At least 2 positive + 2 negative fixtures (or composed-oracle equivalents if upstream fixtures unavailable)
- [ ] Tests pass
- [ ] CHANGELOG entry in `pkix-profiles-cabf`

## Out of scope

- Other tiers (PKIX-jbvb.1 Organization, PKIX-jbvb.2 Sponsor)
- Real-world identity-proofing logic — Profile validates the cert AS IF the CA correctly proofed the subscriber; the BR's proofing requirements are CA-side, not validator-side

